   902	**4.3** **Accuracy Evaluation**
   903	
   904	
   905	As different package manager uses different dependency resolution strategy, there is no standard resolution accuracy benchmark.
   906	For evaluation, we select _Cargo Tree_ tool from the official package
   907	manager _Cargo-1.63.0_ for comparison. We resolve four types of dependency: build, common, optional, and target. Only development
   908	dependencies are omitted as they will not affect the runtime of programs, which is the same as our resolution rules. We first download
   909	source code from the official database _Crates.io_, and then use _Cargo_
   910	_Tree_ to resolve dependencies in the real environment. After that, we
   911	will compare dependency items from _Cargo Tree_ and our ecosystem
   912	dependency graph. To evaluate accuracy in the different data sets,
   913	we select 2000 packages from the whole ecosystem as our standard
   914	dependency benchmark data set and choose three strategies to
   915	select these packages: 1) Random: Randomly selected versions. 2)
   916	Popular: Latest versions of packages that have the most downloads.
   917	3) Mostdep: Latest versions of packages that have the most direct
   918	dependencies, which is the most complex situation a resolver will
   919	meet. We select the latest versions of the given package because
   920	it is chosen to be the dependency package version by default and
   921	typically has the most complex dependencies.
